The following implementations of kmeans.py, hclustering.py, and dbscan.py
all of which utilize imported functions from files we had to create as helper
functions and metric functions in order to make computations.

Here are the files that will be included in the Lab04.zip deliverables:
// kmeans.py
// hclustering.py
// dbscan.py
// helpers.py ** additional file
// metrics.py ** additional file

What is helpers.py?
// implements a "load_clustering_data" function to essentially load in data
from the CSV files that were included in the assignment's spec (which will be the input).
// implements an "euclidean_distance" function to perform euclidean distance
// implements a "compute_distance_matrix" function to compute a corresponding distance matrix
// implements a "compute_centroid" function to compute a corresponding centroid
// implements a "cluster_radius" to compute the cluster's radius relative to the centroid
// implements an "intercluster_distance" function to compute distances between clusters

What is metrics.py?
// implements a "compute_silhouette" function to compute a given point's silhouette score
// implements a "compute_cluster_silhouettes" function to compute a cluster's silhouette scores
// implements an "intercluster_distance" function to compute the intercluster distance between two clusters
// implements a "radius_distance_ratio" function to compute the ratio (helpful when comparing to silhouette scores in algorithms)
// implements a "compute_rand_index" function to compute the rand_index/ rand_score

When testing for certain values (epsilons, minpts, k, etc.) were tested by testing a range of values to
determine which provided the "best" clustering (specifically by comparing between silhouette scores and radius/distance ratios).